'''Gabriel Lourenzo''' "'''Gabi'''" '''Bortoleto Oliveira''' ({{IPA|pt-br|ɡabɾiˈɛw lo(w)ˈɾẽsu boɾtoˈletu oliˈve(j)ɾɐ|lang}}; born 14 October 2004) is a Brazilian [[racing driver]] who competes in [[Formula One]] for [[Audi in Formula One|Audi]].

Born and raised in [[Osasco]], Bortoleto began competitive [[kart racing]] aged seven, winning multiple national titles and graduating to [[formula racing|junior formulae]] in 2020. A [[mentorship|protégé]] of two-time [[List of Formula One World Drivers' Champions|World Drivers' Champion]] [[Fernando Alonso]], Bortoleto became a race-winner in [[2020 Italian F4 Championship|Italian F4]] and [[2022 Formula Regional European Championship|Formula Regional European]], before winning his first title at the [[2023 FIA Formula 3 Championship]] with [[Trident Motorsport|Trident]]. Bortoleto progressed to [[FIA Formula 2]] in {{F2|2024}}, winning the championship that year with [[Invicta Racing|Invicta]] to become the seventh driver in history to win the [[GP2 Series|GP2]]/Formula 2 title in their rookie season; at the [[2024 Monza Formula 2 round|Monza feature race]], Bortoleto became the first driver to win from last on the grid in either Formula 2 or Formula One.

A member of the [[McLaren Driver Development Programme]] from 2023 to 2024, Bortoleto joined [[Sauber]] for {{F1|2025}}, ahead of their acquisition by [[Audi in Formula One|Audi]] in {{F1|2026}}; he achieved several [[List of Formula One points scoring systems|points finishes]] in his rookie season. Bortoleto is contracted to remain at Audi until at least the end of the 2026 season.

== Early and personal life ==
Gabriel Lourenzo Bortoleto Oliveira was born on 14 October 2004 in [[Osasco]], São Paulo, Brazil.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Biografia |url=https://www.gabrielbortoleto.com.br/biografia/ |access-date=29 December 2024 |website=gabrielbortoleto.com.br |language=pt}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Entrevista com o piloto de automobilismo Gabriel Bortoleto - The Noite (04/11/24)|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q1pJ276MuGk|access-date=9 September 2024|website=Youtube|date=4 November 2024}}</ref> His father, Lincoln Oliveira, serves as [[chief executive officer]] and co-owner of the [[Stock Car Pro Series]] in Brazil.<ref name="7Facts">{{Cite web |url=https://motorsport.uol.com.br/f1/news/conheca-curiosidades-sobre-gabriel-bortoleto-novo-piloto-do-brasil-na-f1/10670959/ |title=Conheça 7 fatos sobre Gabriel Bortoleto, novo piloto do Brasil na F1 |trans-title=Discover 7 facts about Gabriel Bortoleto, Brazil's new F1 driver |last=Costa |first=Carlos |date=6 November 2024 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=16 December 2024}}</ref> He founded ''Americanet'' in 1996, which merged with ''Vero'' in 2023 to become one of the largest [[internet service provider]]s in Brazil, with a revenue of {{currency|1.9|BRL}} billion ({{currency|380|USD}} million).<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.bnamericas.com/en/news/vero-americanet-conclude-merger-and-generate-19bn-real-revenue-business |title=Vero, Americanet conclude merger and generate 1.9bn-real revenue business |date=4 December 2023 |website=BNamericas |access-date=16 December 2024}}</ref>

The family also operates ''[[KTF Sports]]'', a [[Stock Car Pro Series]] and [[kart racing]] team.<ref name="7Facts"/> His older brother, Enzo, formerly competed in [[GB3 Championship|BRDC British Formula 3]].<ref name="7Facts"/> Bortoleto is known as "Bibi" amongst his close friends.<ref name="7Facts"/> He is managed by ''A14 Management'', a firm owned by [[Fernando Alonso]], and his career is supported by [[Porto Seguro S.A.|Porto Seguro]], [[O Boticário]], [[Banco de Brasília]], and [[Qualcomm Snapdragon]].<ref name="7Facts"/> He has been dating [[computer science]] student Isabella Bernardini since 2020.<ref name="7Facts"/> His racing idol is [[Ayrton Senna]].<ref name="7Facts"/>

== Junior racing career ==
=== Karting (2011–2019) ===
Bortoleto began [[karting]] in October 2011.<ref name="F3 Interview">{{Cite web |url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/682BBPvCmTr7oWUx3re7cT/gabriel-bortoleto-my-greatest-influences |title=Gabriel Bortoleto: My Greatest Influences |date=15 June 2023 |website=[[FIA Formula 3 Championship]] |access-date=16 December 2024}}</ref> Bortoleto started competing in the Campeonato Sulbrasileiro de Kart in 2012. At the age of eleven, he moved to Europe to pursue a racing career with support from his family.<ref name="F3 Interview"/> He remained in karts until 2019, with his most successful year being 2018, where he finished third in the [[CIK-FIA Karting European Championship|European]] and [[Karting World Championship|World Championships]] in [[OK-Junior]], and became vice-champion in both the [[WSK Super Master Series]] and the [[Andrea Margutti Trophy]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=The top karting stars of 2018|url=https://formulascout.com/the-top-karting-stars-of-2018/46953|access-date=28 April 2021|website=formulascout.com|date=26 December 2018 |language=en}}</ref>

=== Formula 4 (2020) ===
Bortoleto made his car racing debut in the [[2020 Italian F4 Championship]], partnering [[Sebastián Montoya]], [[Gabriele Minì]] and [[Dino Beganovic]] at [[Prema Powerteam]].<ref>{{cite web|date=10 December 2019|title=Gabriel Bortoleto closes with PREMA and will compete in F4 in Europe – Other Categories|url=https://www.time24.news/2019/12/gabriel-bortoleto-closes-with-prema-and-will-compete-in-f4-in-europe-other-categories.html|access-date=27 December 2019|archive-date=27 December 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191227105106/https://www.time24.news/2019/12/gabriel-bortoleto-closes-with-prema-and-will-compete-in-f4-in-europe-other-categories.html|url-status=dead}}</ref> His first podium came at [[Mugello Circuit|Mugello]], where he scored second, third, and a victory, taking his first single-seater win in the fourth round of the season.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Prema's Gabriel Bortoleto claims first Italian F4 win at Mugello|url=https://formulascout.com/premas-gabriel-bortoleto-claims-first-italian-f4-win-at-mugello/69120|access-date=28 April 2021|website=formulascout.com|date=4 October 2020 |language=en}}</ref> He scored two more podiums in [[Autodromo Nazionale di Monza|Monza]] and finished the season fifth in the overall championship, ahead of Montoya but behind Beganovic and eventual champion Minì. Bortoleto also finished fourth in the rookies' standings.{{citation needed|date=March 2023}}

=== Formula Regional (2021–2022) ===
==== 2021: Rookie campaign and first podium ====
[[File:FREC 2021 Spielberg Nr. 85 Bortoleto.jpg|thumb|left|Bortoleto racing in the [[2021 Formula Regional European Championship]] at the [[Red Bull Ring]].]]
In March 2021, it was announced that Bortoleto would be making his debut in the [[2021 Formula Regional European Championship|Formula Regional European Championship]] with [[Fernando Alonso|FA Racing]], run by [[MP Motorsport]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Allen|first=Peter|date=15 April 2021|title=Gabriel Bortoleto makes FA Racing switch before FREC opener|url=https://formulascout.com/gabriel-bortoleto-makes-fa-racing-switch-before-frec-opener/77529|access-date=15 April 2021|website=Formula Scout|language=en-US}}</ref> He scored his first points in the first race of the season in Imola, where he finished ninth.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Imola, Race 1 report: Vidales, Quinn and David|url=https://formularegionaleubyalpine.com/imola-race-1-report-vidales-quinn-and-david/|access-date=24 April 2021|website=formularegionaleubyalpine.com|date=17 April 2021 |language=en}}</ref> From there it took until the seventh round at the [[Red Bull Ring]] until Bortoleto scored again — this time claiming a podium in the second race.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Brittle |first=Cian |date=16 September 2021 |title=Saucy gets eighth FREC win, 16 drivers penalised |url=https://formulascout.com/saucy-gets-eighth-frec-win-16-drivers-penalised/83837 |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> This began a run of top-ten finishes, resulting in 15th place in the standings at the end of the year.

==== 2022: Maiden victories with R-ace GP ====
[[File:FREC 2022 Spielberg Nr. 85 (1).jpg|thumb|right|Bortoleto racing in the [[2022 Formula Regional European Championship]] at the [[Red Bull Ring]].]]
After competing for 3Y by [[R-ace GP]] in a partial campaign of the [[2022 Formula Regional Asian Championship|Formula Regional Asian Championship]] at the start of 2022, where he won in a reversed-top-ten race at [[Yas Marina Circuit|Yas Marina]], Bortoleto was announced to join R-ace GP ahead of the [[2022 Formula Regional European Championship|European Championship]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=7 January 2022 |title=R-ace GP signs Bortoleto for FREC, Buhler for FRAC |url=https://formulascout.com/r-ace-gp-signs-bortoleto-for-frec-buhler-for-frac/88390 |access-date=7 January 2022 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-GB}}</ref> While Bortoleto suffered with engine problems at times during the year, he managed to win at [[Circuit de Spa-Francorchamps|Spa]], inheriting victory after teammate [[Hadrien David]] was penalised, and at [[Circuit de Barcelona-Catalunya|Barcelona]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lloyd |first=Martin |date=8 December 2024 |title=F2 champion Bortoleto: FR Europe struggles 'made me a better person, a better driver' |url=https://feederseries.net/2024/12/08/f2-champion-bortoleto-fr-europe-struggles-made-me-a-better-person-a-better-driver/ |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Gascoigne |first=Roger |date=30 July 2022 |title=Bortoleto inherits FREC win as David penalised for safety car pass |url=https://formulascout.com/bortoleto-inherits-frec-win-as-david-penalised-for-safety-car-pass/96938 |access-date=25 October 2022 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=16 October 2022 |title=Bortoleto wins at Barcelona as FREC title fight goes to final round |url=https://formulascout.com/bortoleto-wins-at-barcelona-as-frec-title-fight-goes-to-final-round/99856 |access-date=26 October 2022 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> He ended up sixth overall, being beaten by David but dispatching other teammate [[Lorenzo Fluxá]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Formula Regional European Championship by Alpine Standings 2022 {{!}} Motorsport Stats |url=https://motorsportstats.com/series/formula-regional-european-championship-by-alpine/standings/2022 |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=motorsportstats.com}}</ref>

=== FIA Formula 3 (2023) ===
[[File:FIA F3 Austria 2023 Nr. 5 Bortoleto (1).jpg|thumb|left|Bortoleto driving the [[Dallara F3 2019]] during the [[2023 Spielberg Formula 3 round]]]]
At the end of September, Bortoleto participated in the [[2022 FIA Formula 3 Championship|2022 FIA Formula 3]] post-season test at [[Circuito de Jerez|Jerez]] with [[Trident Racing|Trident]], partnering [[Oliver Goethe]] and [[Leonardo Fornaroli]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Formula 3 returns to action with post-season testing in Jerez|date= 20 September 2022|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/3OrwkHqGy8GUOqEQnmQDT2/formula-3-returns-to-action-with-post-season-testing-in-jerez|access-date=20 September 2022|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Jerez post-season testing Day 2 entry list|date=21 September 2022|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/1PumIQq3VXG9xdujzt4u7U/jerez-post-season-testing-day-2-entry-list|access-date=23 September 2022|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Jerez post-season testing Day 3 entry list|date=22 September 2022|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/263AL5rKdQIzUdm0BOxc2F/jerez-post-season-testing-day-3-entry-list|access-date=23 September 2022|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> Shortly afterwards, he was announced as a Trident driver for the [[2023 FIA Formula 3 Championship]], becoming the first driver to be announced to a team for that season.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://formulascout.com/alonso-protege-gabriel-bortoleto-graduates-to-fia-f3-with-trident/99133|title=Alonso protege Gabriel Bortoleto graduates to FIA F3 with Trident|website=formulascout.com|first=Ida|last=Wood|date=26 September 2022|accessdate=27 September 2022}}</ref>

In his first race at the [[Bahrain International Circuit]], Bortoleto was penalised for causing a collision with [[Rafael Villagómez]] and was classified outside the points. This was followed by a victory in the following day's feature race when first-place finisher [[Gabriele Minì]] received a penalty. Having been elevated to an early championship lead, the Brazilian extended it at [[2023 Melbourne Formula 3 round|Albert Park]] by claiming pole position and a second consecutive feature race victory. He continued to score points in each race of the subsequent five rounds, even achieving a second place during the feature race at the [[Red Bull Ring]] and two runner-up finishes during the sprint races in [[2023 Silverstone Formula 3 round|Britain]] and [[2023 Budapest Formula 3 round|Hungary]].

Sitting on a comfortable lead at the top of the standings, Bortoleto would proceed to have his first non-scoring race of 2023 at [[2023 Spa-Francorchamps Formula 3 round|Spa-Francorchamps]], as a weak qualifying session was followed by contact caused by [[Dino Beganovic]] during Saturday's race, forcing the Brazilian to stop his car.<ref>{{Cite web |date=29 July 2023 |title=Beganovic handed penalty for Bortoleto Spa F3 sprint clash |url=https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/beganovic-handed-penalty-for-bortoleto-spa-f3-sprint-clash/10501947/ |access-date=9 August 2023 |website=www.autosport.com |language=en}}</ref> Despite narrowly missing out on points in Sunday's race, a weak round from all of his immediate title rivals left Bortoleto with a 38-point advantage heading into the final round of the season.<ref>{{Cite web |title=FEATURE RACE: Barnard takes maiden F3 win with Bortoleto two points short of title |url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/6vfDiYRNu6WYexB6XQo8uD/feature-race-barnard-takes-maiden-f3-win-with-bortoleto-two-points-short-of |access-date=9 August 2023 |website=FIAFormula3® - The Official F3® Website |language=en}}</ref> As [[Paul Aron]] and [[Pepe Martí]] missed out on pole position during [[2023 Monza Formula 3 round|Monza]] qualifying, Bortoleto was crowned FIA Formula 3 champion on Friday.<ref>{{Cite web |title=QUALIFYING: Goethe claims maiden pole as Bortoleto seals Championship title |url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/xdZIHv7Rgup5zKNS3u2UV/qualifying-goethe-claims-maiden-pole-as-bortoleto-seals-championship-title |access-date=5 September 2023 |website=FIAFormula3® - The Official F3® Website |language=en}}</ref>

=== FIA Formula 2 (2024) ===
Bortoleto entered [[FIA Formula 2|Formula 2]] for his [[2024 Formula 2 Championship|2024 campaign]], joining [[Invicta Racing]] alongside [[Alpine Academy]] driver [[Kush Maini]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Invicta Virtuosi Racing announce Gabriel Bortoleto and Kush Maini for 2024 season|date=27 November 2023|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/6y9ch1ow8QLQhBrdKvlQyB/invicta-virtuosi-racing-announce-gabriel-bortoleto-and-kush-maini-for-2024|access-date=27 November 2023|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> He began the season by qualifying second for the season opener in [[2024 Sakhir Formula 2 round|Bahrain]] but was promoted to pole position after Maini was disqualified for a technical infringement. He scored points in both races, despite making contact with and spinning around [[Isack Hadjar]] at the start of the feature race.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Maloney completes Bahrain double after winning Feature Race |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/f2-maloney-completes-bahrain-double-after-claiming-feature-race-victory.1iLsreoVGLIVCFk7AyTei2 |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref> At the next round in [[2024 Jeddah Formula 2 round|Jeddah]] Bortoleto qualified 15th, finished tenth in the sprint and retired on lap 1 of the feature race with a driveshaft failure.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Invicta Racing picks up first podium of 2024 at Jeddah |url=https://invictaracing.com/post/2024-fia-formula-2-jeddah-feature-race-report |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=Invicta Racing |language=en}}</ref> He also retired from the sprint race at [[2024 Melbourne Formula 2 round|Melbourne]] after being sent into the wall by [[Pepe Martí]], who had been squeezed by Hadjar at the start, and also failed to finish the feature race due to a hydraulic failure.<ref name=":MLBpen">{{cite web |date=23 March 2024 |title=Isack Hadjar loses Sprint Race win, Bearman and Crawford also penalised |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/4BmF0R0l1XqWdKfUPy0Ycg/isack-hadjar-loses-sprint-race-win-bearman-and-crawford-penalised |access-date=23 March 2024 |website=FIAFormula2® - The Official F2® Website}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Walton |first=Steven |date=11 May 2024 |title=Bortoleto 'happy that the pace is there' in F2 |url=https://feederseries.net/2024/05/11/bortoleto-happy-that-the-pace-is-there-in-f2/ |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref>

Bortoleto bounced back by taking pole for the round in [[2024 Imola Formula 2 round|Imola]] and scoring his first points since Bahrain during the sprint, finishing sixth.<ref>{{Cite web |title=F2: Bortoleto takes last gasp pole ahead of Bearman |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/f2-bortoleto-takes-last-gasp-pole-position-ahead-of-bearman-in-imola.7iuwlvDheYMLpMyZdeYlk0 |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref> Though he fell down to fourth at the start of Sunday's event, Bortoleto moved back to second after the pit stop phase; he chased down Hadjar but could not pass him before the race ended, claiming his first podium in F2 with second place.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lawrence |first=Dan |date=19 May 2024 |title=Hadjar thwarts Borteleto to take F2 Imola Feature Race win |url=https://www.motorsportweek.com/2024/05/19/hadjar-thwarts-borteleto-to-take-f2-imola-feature-race-win/ |access-date=20 December 2024 |website=Motorsport Week |language=en-GB}}</ref> He then qualified ninth in [[2024 Monte Carlo Formula 2 round|Monaco]] and finished the sprint race in second, having started from the front row due to the reverse-top-ten format.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Solanki |first=Shayni |date=25 May 2024 |title=Rookie Barnard lands maiden F2 win in Monaco Sprint |url=https://www.motorsportweek.com/2024/05/25/rookie-barnard-lands-maiden-f2-win-in-monaco-sprint/ |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=Motorsport Week |language=en-GB}}</ref> He then finished the feature in eighth. More points followed in both [[2024 Barcelona Formula 2 round|Barcelona]] races, though Bortoleto was demoted from seventh to tenth in the feature after causing a collision with his teammate on the final lap.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Bortoleto handed post-Feature Race penalty |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/3XfE50kRB9pQL6udJDxx8E/bortoleto-handed-post-feature-race-penalty |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref>

[[File:FIA F2 Austria 2024 Nr. 10 Bortoleto.jpg|thumb|Bortoleto became the fourth driver to win [[FIA Formula 3]] and [[FIA Formula 2]] in successive years.]]

In [[2024 Spielberg Formula 2 round|Austria]], Bortoleto qualified fourth and progressed from eighth to fourth during the sprint race, though he narrowly lost out on a podium to [[Paul Aron]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lawrence |first=Dan |date=29 June 2024 |title=Bearman turns his luck with Formula 2 Austria Sprint victory |url=https://www.motorsportweek.com/2024/06/29/bearman-turns-his-luck-with-formula-2-austria-sprint-victory/ |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=Motorsport Week |language=en-GB}}</ref> On Sunday, Bortoleto passed race leader [[Joshua Dürksen]] on lap 4 and later overtook Martí, who had jumped him by pitting during a virtual safety car, to claim his maiden F2 victory and enter the top three in the championship.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lloyd |first=Martin |date=1 July 2024 |title=Bortoleto finally wins, and Campos teammates battle: 5 key takeaways from F2 at Spielberg |url=https://feederseries.net/2024/07/01/bortoleto-finally-wins-and-campos-teammates-battle-5-key-takeaways-from-f2-at-spielberg/ |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=30 June 2024 |title=McLaren's Bortoleto Wins Austrian Feature Race as Team Orders Cause Controversy - Formula 2 |url=https://www.insidef2.com/mclarens-bortoleto-wins-austrian-feature-race-as-team-orders-cause-controversy/ |access-date=25 December 2024 |language=en-GB}}</ref> He progressed further with two points results at [[2024 Silverstone Formula 2 round|Silverstone]] but was penalised again due to a battle with Maini, this time being demoted from third to fourth after a last-lap overtake was judged to have happened off-track.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lopez |first=Alejandro Alonso |date=6 July 2024 |title=Bortoleto penalised after intense F2 fight with Maini and loses podium |url=https://formulascout.com/bortoleto-penalised-after-intense-f2-fight-with-maini-and-loses-podium/121044 |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> In the [[2024 Budapest Formula 2 round|Budapest]] sprint race Bortoleto struggled with tyre wear on his soft tyres, dropping to 16th, and finished fourth in the feature race after losing the podium to [[Richard Verschoor]] on the final lap.<ref>{{Cite web |title=2024 FIA Formula 2 Hungary Sprint Race results |url=https://invictaracing.com/post/2024-fia-formula-2-hungary-sprint-race-results |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=Invicta Racing |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=F2: Antonelli storms through to take victory in Budapest |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/f2-antonelli-storms-through-to-take-victory-in-budapest-feature-race.5A2J07qi74NZmMKgT9LXN0 |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref> For the final round before the summer break in [[2024 Spa-Francorchamps Formula 2 round|Belgium]] Bortoleto qualified second and fought for the victory with Hadjar, eventually ending up second and moving up to said place in the standings after a late technical issue ended Aron's race.<ref>{{Cite web |title=F2: Hadjar extends title advantage with fourth win of 2024 |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/f2-hadjar-extends-title-advantage-with-fourth-win-of-2024.7pMkJB2LfLM9FMs4cZK7dN |access-date=20 December 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref>

Bortoleto's start to the [[2024 Monza Formula 2 round|Monza]] round was a disaster: he spun in qualifying before setting a time, therefore necessitating a start from last place for both races.<ref>{{Cite web |title=QUALIFYING: Maloney beats Hadjar to take maiden F2 pole position in Monza |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/23hfDSdeAUapjehlhLGXKZ/qualifying-maloney-beats-hadjar-to-take-maiden-f2-pole-position-in-monza |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref> In the sprint race, Bortoleto charged through to eighth, sharing the final point with [[Dennis Hauger]] after crossing the finish line in a [[dead heat]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=SPRINT RACE: Bearman dominates to take victory in entertaining Monza battle |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/5kIbLWZBIQ3ztEPtz0iKuN/sprint-race-bearman-dominates-to-take-victory-in-entertaining-monza-battle |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref> It would however be the feature race where Bortoleto experienced his standout result of the entire year: he benefited from an opportune safety car, which, following his pit stop, allowed him to stay ahead of all drivers who had stopped prior to its deployment. Bortoleto drove out a gap to take a last-to-first victory and benefited from Hadjar's scoreless weekend to close up in the championship.<ref>{{Cite web |title=F2: Bortoleto reigns in Monza as he goes from last to first |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/f2-bortoleto-reigns-in-monza-as-he-goes-from-last-to-first-in-feature-race.5khZHJnXPkKmlKKpTyitj5 |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref> He became the first driver to win from last on the grid in Formula 2.<ref>{{Cite web|title=How the "stars aligned" for Bortoleto's stunning last-to-first F2 victory|url=https://www.autosport.com/formula2/news/how-the-stars-aligned-for-bortoletos-stunning-last-to-first-f2-victory/10650691/#:~:text=Well-timed%20safety%20car%20stop,on%20points%20leader%20Isack%20Hadjar&text=Gabriel%20Bortoleto%20stunned%20the%20Formula,from%20last%20on%20the%20grid.|access-date=9 September 2024|website=Autosport|date=2 September 2024 |language=en}}</ref> This performance later earned him the [[Mecachrome]] Outstanding Win Award at the end-of-year prize giving ceremony.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Gabriel Bortoleto wins Mecachrome Outstanding Win Award for Monza Feature Race victory |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/4BqDtNQZPnSLlr6eSP5CEZ/gabriel-bortoleto-wins-mecachrome-outstanding-win-award-for-monza-feature |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref>

In the [[2024 Baku Formula 2 round|Baku]] round, Bortoleto finished the sprint race in fifth place and the main race in fourth, taking the lead in the drivers' championship by 4.5 points over Hadjar.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lloyd |first=Martin |date=17 September 2024 |title=Bortoleto takes points lead as Verschoor wins: 5 key takeaways from F2 in Baku |url=https://feederseries.net/2024/09/17/bortoleto-leads-whilst-verschoor-celebrates-5-key-takeaways-from-f2-in-baku/ |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref> Bortoleto qualified second in [[2024 Lusail Formula 2 round|Qatar]] and finished fifth on Saturday. He then took the lead from Aron at the start of the feature race, only to be penalised for crossing the pit entry line behind the pit bollard when avoiding the pit lane entrance during a virtual safety car deployment. Though he progressed through the pack and crossed the line in first, Bortoleto was demoted behind Aron and Hadjar in the results, meaning that he and Hadjar would go into the season finale with a gap of half a point.<ref>{{Cite web |date=1 December 2024 |title=Aron wins in Qatar after penalty drops Bortoleto down to third - Formula 2 |url=https://www.insidef2.com/aron-wins-in-qatar-after-penalty-drops-bortoleto-down-to-third/ |access-date=25 December 2024 |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Bortoleto vs Hadjar – the closest title fight in F2 history |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/f2-gabriel-bortoleto-vs-isack-hadjar-the-closest-title-fight-in-history.5CirI9sDN0kmyryCkbfTlS |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref>

Bortoleto qualified second again on [[2024 Yas Island Formula 2 round|Yas Island]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Will |date=6 December 2024 |title=Martins beats title rivals Bortoleto, Aron and Hadjar to Yas Marina pole |url=https://www.racefans.net/2024/12/06/martins-beats-title-rivals-bortoleto-aron-and-hadjar-to-yas-marina-pole/ |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=RaceFans |language=en-GB}}</ref> A charge from ninth to second in the sprint allowed him to enter the final race with a four-point advantage, as Hadjar finished fifth.<ref>{{Cite web |date=7 December 2024 |title=SPRINT RACE: Martí dominates at Yas Marina as Bortoleto extends Championship lead |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/46Y1roZnfUdtp5Mv4BdpL/sprint-race-marti-dominates-at-yas-marina-as-bortoleto-extends-championship |access-date=7 December 2024 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref> The start of the feature race decided the championship fight, as Hadjar stalled on the grid. Bortoleto meanwhile took the lead from [[Victor Martins]] at turn one and although he was later overtaken by Dürksen following the pit stop phase, Bortoleto finished second and was crowned Formula 2 champion.<ref>{{Cite web |date=8 December 2024 |title=FEATURE: Bortoleto crowned Champion after finishing second to Duerksen |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/2ol3EJemGwRBldwxwi4idg/feature-bortoleto-crowned-champion-after-finishing-second-to-duerksen |access-date=8 December 2024 |website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website |language=en}}</ref> He became the fourth champion in the FIA Formula 2 era to win the FIA F3 and F2 titles in successive years, following [[Charles Leclerc]], [[George Russell (racing driver)|George Russell]], and [[Oscar Piastri]], as well as the second Brazilian to triumph in the category after [[Felipe Drugovich]] in [[2022 Formula 2 Championship|2022]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lloyd |first=Martin |date=9 December 2024 |title=Champion Bortoleto finds glory as Hadjar rues stall: Abu Dhabi F2 takeaways |url=https://feederseries.net/2024/12/09/champion-bortoleto-finds-glory-as-hadjar-rues-stall-abu-dhabi-f2-takeaways/ |access-date=25 December 2024 |website=Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref>

== Formula One career ==
In September 2022, Bortoleto announced that he had joined A14, two time [[List of Formula One World Drivers' Champions|Formula One champion]] [[Fernando Alonso]]'s driver management company.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=15 September 2022|title=FRegional racer Gabriel Bortoleto joins Alonso's management company|url=https://formulascout.com/fregional-racer-gabriel-bortoleto-joins-alonsos-management-company/98747|access-date=30 September 2022|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> After winning the [[2023 FIA Formula 3 Championship|Formula 3 title]], Bortoleto signed with the [[McLaren Driver Development Programme]] in October 2023.<ref>{{Cite web|title=McLaren Racing sign FIA Formula 3 Champion Gabriel Bortoleto to the Driver Development programme|date=5 October 2023|url=https://www.mclaren.com/racing/formula-1/2023/mclaren-announce-fia-formula-3-champion-gabriel-bortoleto-as-the-latest-driver-to-join-the-driver-development-programme/|access-date=5 October 2023|publisher=[[McLaren]]|website=mclaren.com|language=en}}</ref> He completed his first test in Formula One machinery at the [[Red Bull Ring]] in September 2024, testing the [[McLaren MCL36]].<ref name="BortoTesto">{{Cite web|title=Gabriel Bortoleto conducts first F1 test with McLaren at Red Bull Ring|url=https://formulascout.com/gabriel-bortoleto-conducts-first-f1-test-with-mclaren-at-red-bull-ring/123451|access-date=9 September 2024|website=formulascout.com|date=7 September 2024 |language=en}}</ref>

Around the time that he completed his first test, [[Sauber Motorsport]] COO and CTO [[Mattia Binotto]] marked Bortoleto as one of the contenders for a seat at Kick Sauber in {{F1|2025}}, ahead of their takeover by [[Audi in Formula One|Audi]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://racingnews365.com/binotto-reveals-two-surprise-options-for-vacant-audi-f1-seat|title=Binotto reveals two surprise options for vacant Audi F1 seat|date=1 September 2024|access-date=3 November 2024}}</ref> Then three-time Formula One world champion [[Max Verstappen]] and race winner [[Oscar Piastri]] endorsed Bortoleto to be selected, with Piastri sharing his experience of not getting a seat immediately after winning the [[2021 Formula 2 Championship]] and his hope that Bortoleto would avoid such a situation.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/id-have-signed-him-already-verstappen-reveals-who-hed-choose-for-sauber-seat.6UD2RZOijsLILqtmG7jsDE|title='I'd have signed him already' – Verstappen reveals who he'd choose for Sauber seat in 2025|date=1 November 2024|access-date=3 November 2024}}</ref> Furthermore, McLaren team principal Andrea Stella revealed he would allow Bortoleto to leave their academy for Sauber if needed, praising him for his performances in his junior career.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/we-wont-stop-him-mclaren-boss-stella-comments-on-junior-driver-bortoletos.6dWWO5y7taJYbVsojobuZL|title='We won't stop him' – McLaren boss Stella comments on junior driver Bortoleto's links to Kick Sauber for 2025|date=2 November 2024|access-date=1 January 2025}}</ref>

=== Sauber / Audi (2025–present) ===
==== 2025: Rookie season with Sauber ====
[[File:2025 Japan GP - Sauber - Gabriel Bortoleto - FP2.jpg|thumb|left|Bortoleto (pictured at the {{F1GP|2025|Japanese}}) debuted in Formula One with [[Sauber]] in {{F1|2025}}, ahead of their acquisition by [[Audi in Formula One|Audi]].|alt=Bortoleto driving the Kick Sauber C45 at the 2025 Japanese Grand Prix]]
Bortoleto signed for [[Sauber]] in {{F1|2025}}, partnering [[Nico Hülkenberg]] on a multi-year deal beyond the [[2026 Formula One World Championship#Regulation changes|2026 regulation changes]] with [[Audi in Formula One|Audi]]; they replaced [[Valtteri Bottas]] and [[Zhou Guanyu]].<ref name="signing">{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/sauber-signs-bortoleto-to-2025-f1-race-seat-ahead-of-audi-era/10671012/ |title=Sauber signs Bortoleto for 2025 F1 race seat ahead of Audi era |last=Vinel |first=Ben |date=6 November 2024 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=15 March 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241113051110/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/sauber-signs-bortoleto-to-2025-f1-race-seat-ahead-of-audi-era/10671012/ |archive-date=13 November 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> He was subsequently released from the [[McLaren Driver Development Programme]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/introducing-f1s-new-rookies-gabriel-bortoleto-aiming-to-be-brazils-next-senna/10701899/ |title=Introducing F1's rookies: How Bortoleto aims to inspire like a previous Brazilian hero |last=Kalinauckas |first=Alex |date=10 March 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=15 March 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250310212612/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/introducing-f1s-new-rookies-gabriel-bortoleto-aiming-to-be-brazils-next-senna/10701899/ |archive-date=10 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> On debut at the {{F1GP|2025|Australian}}, Bortoleto received acclaim for progressing to the second qualifying session, outqualifying teammate Hülkenberg;<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/f1-australia-gp-live-updates-qualifying-fp3-times-results/QMkxXu5TpiPX/KS0UpH2il7Du/ |title=Classy work from Bortoleto |last=Bailey |first=Michael |date=15 March 2025 |work=[[The Athletic]] |publisher=[[The New York Times]] |access-date=15 March 2025 |issn=1553-8095 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250315184909/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/f1-australia-gp-live-updates-qualifying-fp3-times-results/QMkxXu5TpiPX/KS0UpH2il7Du/ |archive-date=15 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/c3d8zre0x9lo |title=Norris takes Melbourne pole with Hamilton eighth |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=15 March 2025 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=15 March 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250315184918/https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/c3d8zre0x9lo |archive-date=15 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> he crashed out of the race in changing conditions.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/cr421xe109qo |title=Norris beats Verstappen in dramatic Australia opener |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=16 March 2025 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=16 March 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250316070859/https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/cr421xe109qo |archive-date=16 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He finished nineteenth in the {{F1GP|2025|Chinese}} sprint following a final-lap collision with [[Jack Doohan]],<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/jack-doohan-hit-with-penalty-after-chinese-sprint-race/10705904/ |title=Jack Doohan hit with penalty after Chinese GP sprint clash with Bortoleto |last=Mee |first=Lydia |date=22 March 2025 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=26 March 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250326163608/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/jack-doohan-hit-with-penalty-after-chinese-sprint-race/10705904/ |archive-date=26 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> before finishing fourteenth in the main race after spinning into the [[gravel trap]] on the opening lap.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/bortoleto-not-proud-of-lap-1-spin-in-china-as-hulkenberg-rues-impact-of.6EqmdQSX5mRISQx4qEm1gf |title=Bortoleto 'not proud' of Lap 1 spin in China as Hulkenberg rues impact of early damage on 'very tricky' day |date=26 March 2025 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=26 March 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250326163605/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/bortoleto-not-proud-of-lap-1-spin-in-china-as-hulkenberg-rues-impact-of.6EqmdQSX5mRISQx4qEm1gf |archive-date=26 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He then finished nineteenth in [[2025 Japanese Grand Prix|Japan]] on an alternate strategy,<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://racer.com/2025/04/06/verstappen-cruises-to-fourth-straight-japanese-gp-win/ |title=Verstappen cruises to fourth straight Japanese GP win |last=Lamonato |first=Michael |date=6 April 2025 |magazine=[[Racer (magazine)|Racer]] |publisher=[[Racer (magazine)|Racer Media & Marketing Inc.]] |access-date=6 April 2025 |issn=1066-6060 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250406180026/https://racer.com/2025/04/06/verstappen-cruises-to-fourth-straight-japanese-gp-win/ |archive-date=6 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> as well as eighteenth in both [[2025 Bahrain Grand Prix|Bahrain]]—where he described the [[Kick Sauber C45|C45]] as "undriveable"—and [[2025 Saudi Arabian Grand Prix|Saudi Arabia]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.cnnbrasil.com.br/esportes/automobilismo/gabriel-bortoleto-detona-carro-da-sauber-apos-gp-do-bahrein-inguiavel/ |title=Gabriel Bortoleto detona carro da Sauber após GP do Bahrein: "Inguiável" |trans-title=Gabriel Bortoleto blasts Sauber's car after Bahrain GP: "Undriveable" |last=Cardoso |first=João Marcelo |date=14 April 2025 |work=[[CNN Brasil]] |publisher=[[CNN]] |language=pt |access-date=15 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250415161837/https://www.cnnbrasil.com.br/esportes/automobilismo/gabriel-bortoleto-detona-carro-da-sauber-apos-gp-do-bahrein-inguiavel/ |archive-date=15 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.espn.com.br/f1/artigo/_/id/15076040/formula-1-piastri-vence-gp-da-arabia-saudita-vira-lider-f1-bortoleto-termina-ultimo |title=F1: Bortoleto termina em último no GP da Arábia Saudita; Piastri vence e vira líder do mundial |trans-title=F1: Bortoleto finishes last in the Saudi Arabian GP; Piastri wins and becomes world championship leader |date=20 April 2025 |website=[[ESPN (Brazil)|ESPN]] |publisher=[[ESPN Inc.]] |language=pt |access-date=21 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250421214059/https://www.espn.com.br/f1/artigo/_/id/15076040/formula-1-piastri-vence-gp-da-arabia-saudita-vira-lider-f1-bortoleto-termina-ultimo |archive-date=21 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Claiming fifteenth in the {{F1GP|2025|Miami}} sprint,<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://ge.globo.com/motor/formula-1/noticia/2025/05/03/gp-de-miami-norris-sobrevive-a-caos-e-vence-corrida-sprint-bortoleto-e-16o.ghtml |title=GP de Miami: Norris aproveita caos e vence corrida sprint; Bortoleto é 15º |trans-title=Miami GP: Norris takes advantage of chaos and wins sprint race; Bortoleto is 15th |date=3 May 2025 |website=[[Globo (media company)|ge]] |publisher=[[Globo (media company)|Globo]] |language=pt |access-date=12 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250505225252/https://ge.globo.com/motor/formula-1/noticia/2025/05/03/gp-de-miami-norris-sobrevive-a-caos-e-vence-corrida-sprint-bortoleto-e-16o.ghtml |archive-date=5 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> he retired from the main race with a fuel system issue whilst running thirteenth.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.cnnbrasil.com.br/esportes/automobilismo/piastri-domina-vence-em-miami-e-dispara-na-lideranca-da-formula-1/ |title=Piastri domina, vence em Miami e dispara na liderança da Fórmula 1 |trans-title=Pistri dominates, wins in Miami and fires into the lead of Formula 1 |last=Cardoso |first=João Marcelo |date=4 May 2025 |work=[[CNN Brasil]] |publisher=[[CNN]] |language=pt |access-date=12 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250607035628/https://www.cnnbrasil.com.br/esportes/automobilismo/piastri-domina-vence-em-miami-e-dispara-na-lideranca-da-formula-1/ |archive-date=7 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He started fourteenth in [[2025 Emilia Romagna Grand Prix|Emilia Romagna]] before dropping to eighteenth on an alternate strategy.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://ge.globo.com/motor/formula-1/noticia/2025/05/18/bortoleto-atribui-18o-lugar-a-azar-com-safety-cars-e-tres-paradas-em-imola.ghtml |title=Bortoleto atribui 18º lugar a azar com safety cars e três paradas em Ímola |trans-title=Bortoleto attributes 18th place to bad luck with safety cars and three stops in Imola |date=18 May 2025 |website=[[Globo (media company)|ge]] |publisher=[[Globo (media company)|Globo]] |language=pt |access-date=12 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250712002831/https://ge.globo.com/motor/formula-1/noticia/2025/05/18/bortoleto-atribui-18o-lugar-a-azar-com-safety-cars-e-tres-paradas-em-imola.ghtml |archive-date=12 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> A first-lap incident with [[Kimi Antonelli]] at ''[[Circuit de Monaco|Portier]]'' saw Bortoleto drop to last in the {{F1GP|2025|Monaco}}; he recovered to fourteenth.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/bortoleto-unhappy-with-risk-antonelli-took-that-resulted-in-crash-after.6jSOx76YDAVch804zQnCph |title=Bortoleto unhappy with 'risk' Antonelli took that resulted in crash after 'embarrassing' overtake |date=27 May 2025 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=12 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250614005655/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/bortoleto-unhappy-with-risk-antonelli-took-that-resulted-in-crash-after.6jSOx76YDAVch804zQnCph |archive-date=14 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.reuters.com/sports/formula1/bortoleto-clarifies-comment-about-putting-antonelli-wall-2025-05-29/ |title=Bortoleto clarifies comment about putting Antonelli in the wall |last=Baldwin |first=Alan |date=29 May 2025 |work=[[Reuters]] |publisher=[[Thomson Reuters]] |access-date=12 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250712003445/https://www.reuters.com/sports/formula1/bortoleto-clarifies-comment-about-putting-antonelli-wall-2025-05-29/ |archive-date=12 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

[[File:FIA F1 Austria 2025 Nr. 5 Bortoleto.jpg|thumb|right|After mid-season upgrades to the [[Kick Sauber C45|C45]], Bortoleto scored his maiden [[List of Formula One World Championship points scoring systems|points finish]] at the {{F1GP|2025|Austrian}}.|alt=Bortoleto driving the Kick Sauber C45 at the 2025 Austrian Grand Prix]]
Upgrades for the {{F1GP|2025|Spanish}} saw Sauber emerge as a [[Glossary of motorsport terms#M|midfield]] challenger, with Bortoleto qualifying and finishing twelfth.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.racecar-engineering.com/articles/f1/updates-that-helped-sauber-log-its-best-result-in-three-years/ |title=Updates that Helped Sauber Log its Best Result in Three Years |last=Lloyd |first=Daniel |date=5 June 2025 |magazine=Racecar Engineering |publisher=The Chelsea Magazine Company |access-date=12 July 2025 |issn=2754-7647 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250618185739/https://www.racecar-engineering.com/articles/f1/updates-that-helped-sauber-log-its-best-result-in-three-years/ |archive-date=18 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/saubers-pinch-yourself-moment-after-nico-hulkenberg-beats-lewis-hamiltons-ferrari/10729319/ |title=Sauber's "pinch yourself moment" after Hulkenberg beats Hamilton's Ferrari |last=Cleeren |first=Filip |date=3 June 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=12 July 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250604020055/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/saubers-pinch-yourself-moment-after-nico-hulkenberg-beats-lewis-hamiltons-ferrari/10729319/ |archive-date=4 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.autohebdo.fr/actualites/f1/je-battais-ces-pilotes-qui-performent-aujourdhui-en-f1-gabriel-bortoleto-sur-son-debut-de-saison.html |title=Gabriel Bortoleto prend son mal en patience : « L'an dernier je battais ces pilotes qui performent aujourd'hui en F1 » |trans-title=Gabriel Bortoleto takes his pain in patience: "Last year, I beat the drivers who are performing in F1" |last=Derckel |first=Hugues |date=11 June 2025 |magazine=Auto Hebdo |language=fr |issn=0395-4366 |access-date=12 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250712022423/https://www.autohebdo.fr/actualites/f1/je-battais-ces-pilotes-qui-performent-aujourdhui-en-f1-gabriel-bortoleto-sur-son-debut-de-saison.html |archive-date=12 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He dropped to fourteenth in [[2025 Canadian Grand Prix|Canada]],<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://motorsport.uol.com.br/f1/news/f1-com-batida-entre-mclarens-russell-domina-e-vence-gp-do-canada-bortoleto-chega-em-14º/10733198/ |title=F1: Com batida entre McLarens, Russell domina e vence GP do Canadá; Bortoleto termina em 14º |trans-title=F1: With crash between McLarens, Russell dominates and wins the Canadian GP; Bortoleto finishes in 14th |last=Gobbo |first=Andrei |date=15 June 2025 |work=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |language=pt |access-date=12 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250712022430/https://motorsport.uol.com.br/f1/news/f1-com-batida-entre-mclarens-russell-domina-e-vence-gp-do-canada-bortoleto-chega-em-14%C2%BA/10733198/ |archive-date=12 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> prior to claiming his maiden [[List of Formula One World Championship points scoring systems|points finish]] in [[2025 Austrian Grand Prix|Austria]]: qualifying eighth, he held position and challenged [[Fernando Alonso]] for seventh in the closing laps, becoming the [[Formula One drivers from Brazil|first Brazilian]] to score points in Formula One since [[2017 Abu Dhabi Grand Prix|2017]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/master-and-apprentice-the-f1-austrian-gp-battle-between-bortoleto-and-boss-alonso/10737949/ |title=Master and apprentice – the F1 Austrian GP battle between Bortoleto and 'boss' Alonso |last=Mann-Bryans |first=Mark |date=30 June 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=12 July 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250701011146/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/master-and-apprentice-the-f1-austrian-gp-battle-between-bortoleto-and-boss-alonso/10737949/ |archive-date=1 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.reuters.com/sports/formula1/bortoleto-hopes-he-can-fight-points-rest-f1-season-2025-06-30/ |title=Bortoleto hopes he can fight for points for rest of F1 season |last=Baldwin |first=Alan |date=30 June 2025 |work=[[Reuters]] |publisher=[[Thomson Reuters]] |access-date=12 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250701071607/https://www.reuters.com/sports/formula1/bortoleto-hopes-he-can-fight-points-rest-f1-season-2025-06-30/ |archive-date=1 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Starting seventeenth at the rain-affected {{F1GP|2025|British}}, he gambled with a [[formation lap]] switch to [[slick tyres]] and crashed out three laps later at ''[[Silverstone Circuit|Farm]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/i-made-a-mistake-bortoleto-explains-error-that-led-to-early-exit-from.6ccXD9rgbVWd7B1hMSaJbf |title='I made a mistake' – Bortoleto explains error that led to early exit from British Grand Prix |date=8 July 2025 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=12 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250712023059/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/i-made-a-mistake-bortoleto-explains-error-that-led-to-early-exit-from.6ccXD9rgbVWd7B1hMSaJbf |archive-date=12 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.metropoles.com/esportes/formula-1-em-corrida-caotica-lando-norris-vence-gp-da-inglaterra |title=Fórmula 1: em corrida caótica, Lando Norris vence GP da Inglaterra |trans-title=Formula 1: in chaotic race, Lando Norris wins the GP of England |last=Silva |first=Cleverton |date=6 July 2025 |work=[[Metrópoles]] |publisher=[[Metrópoles|Grupo Metrópoles de Comunicação]] |language=pt |issn=1957-7788 |access-date=12 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250712023103/https://www.metropoles.com/esportes/formula-1-em-corrida-caotica-lando-norris-vence-gp-da-inglaterra |archive-date=12 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He claimed ninth in both the sprint and wet–dry Grand Prix in [[2025 Belgian Grand Prix|Belgium]],<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.estadao.com.br/esportes/velocidade/bortoleto-preve-gp-belga-complicado-e-verstappen-espera-segurar-mclaren-como-gato-e-rato/ |title=Bortoleto prevê GP belga 'complicado' e Verstappen espera segurar McLaren: 'Como gato e rato' |trans-title=Bortoleto predicts 'complicated' Belgian GP and Verstappen hopes to chase McLaren: 'As a cat and rat' |date=26 July 2025 |work=[[O Estado de S. Paulo]] |publisher=[[O Estado de S. Paulo|Grupo Estado]] |language=pt |issn=1516-2931 |access-date=2 August 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250802153140/https://www.estadao.com.br/esportes/velocidade/bortoleto-preve-gp-belga-complicado-e-verstappen-espera-segurar-mclaren-como-gato-e-rato/ |archive-date=2 August 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/bortoleto-feels-like-i-did-everything-to-reach-p9-at-spa-as-hulkenberg.5MMbfBZnQXjdA4btkE6D9H |title=Bortoleto feels 'like I did everything' to reach P9 at Spa as Hulkenberg targets Hungary points |date=30 July 2025 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=2 August 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250802153304/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/bortoleto-feels-like-i-did-everything-to-reach-p9-at-spa-as-hulkenberg.5MMbfBZnQXjdA4btkE6D9H |archive-date=2 August 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> as well as seventh in qualifying for the {{F1GP|2025|Hungarian}}, where he held off [[Lance Stroll]] for sixth; Bortoleto had stayed past [[curfew#Sport|curfew]] on the Friday to adjust his setup with his [[race engineer|engineers]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.uol.com.br/esporte/ultimas-noticias/2025/08/03/gp-da-hungria.htm |title=Norris segura Piastri e vence na Hungria em melhor prova de Bortoleto na F1 |trans-title=Norris holds Piastri and wins in Hungary in Bortoleto's best F1 race |last=Cerasoli |first=Julianne |date=3 August 2025 |work=[[Universo Online]] |publisher=[[Grupo Folha]] |language=pt |access-date=4 August 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250804185016/https://www.uol.com.br/esporte/ultimas-noticias/2025/08/03/gp-da-hungria.htm |archive-date=4 August 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/jonathan-wheatley-hails-future-star-gabriel-bortoleto-after-sauber-broke-curfew-at-hungarian-gp/10748519/ |title=Jonathan Wheatley hails "future star" Gabriel Bortoleto after Sauber broke curfew at Hungarian GP |last1=Mee |first1=Lydia |last2=Cleeren |first2=Filip |date=4 August 2025 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=4 August 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250804185023/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/jonathan-wheatley-hails-future-star-gabriel-bortoleto-after-sauber-broke-curfew-at-hungarian-gp/10748519/ |archive-date=4 August 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He claimed fifteenth in the [[2025 Dutch Grand Prix|Netherlands]] after dropping to last with a slow start and a strategic error,<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/winners-and-losers-from-f1s-pivotal-dutch-grand-prix/10755219 |title=Winners and losers from F1's pivotal Dutch Grand Prix |last=Cleeren |first=Filip |date=31 August 2025 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=20 September 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250910012455/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/winners-and-losers-from-f1s-pivotal-dutch-grand-prix/10755219 |archive-date=10 September 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> before starting seventh and finishing eighth in [[2025 Italian Grand Prix|Italy]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/2025-f1-italian-grand-prix-driver-rankings-edd-straw |title=Edd Straw's 2025 Italian Grand Prix F1 driver rankings |last=Straw |first=Edd |date=8 September 2025 |website=The Race |publisher=The Race Media |access-date=20 September 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250920192113/https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/2025-f1-italian-grand-prix-driver-rankings-edd-straw/ |archive-date=20 September 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Whilst battling [[Alexander Albon]] for tenth in the [[2025 São Paulo Grand Prix|São Paulo]] sprint, he suffered a {{Convert|57|g-force|lk=on|abbr=|m/s2 ft/s2}} barrier collision at the ''[[Interlagos Circuit|Senna 'S']]'', forcing him to miss qualifying for his home Grand Prix.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://motorsport.uol.com.br/f1/news/f1-bortoleto-nao-participa-da-classificacao-para-o-gp-de-sao-paulo-apos-batida-na-sprint/10775022 |title=F1: Bortoleto não participa da classificação para o GP de São Paulo após batida na sprint |trans-title=F1: Bortoleto does not participate in qualifying for the São Paulo GP after crash in the sprint |last=Longo |first=Guilherme |date=8 November 2025 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |language=pt |access-date=8 November 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251108193322/https://motorsport.uol.com.br/f1/news/f1-bortoleto-nao-participa-da-classificacao-para-o-gp-de-sao-paulo-apos-batida-na-sprint/10775022/ |archive-date=8 November 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> After starting from the last place on the grid at the São Paulo Grand Prix, he recovered some places before being tapped by Lance Stroll's [[Aston Martin in Formula One|Aston Martin]] marking an early end to his home race.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/bortoleto-evaluates-one-of-the-toughest-weekends-after-double-crash-in-first.7q3UaRQkyAO2zAVU5YtIod |title=Bortoleto evaluates 'one of the toughest weekends' after double crash in first home event |date=8 November 2025 |website=Formula 1 |publisher=Formula One World Championship Limited |access-date=11 November 2025 |language=en}}</ref>

==== 2026: Audi ====
[[File:Gabriel Bortoleto British Grand Prix 2026.jpg|thumb|Bortoleto driving through Becketts corner for [[Audi in Formula One|Audi Revolut F1 Team]] at the [[2026 British Grand Prix]]]]
Bortoleto was contracted to retain his place alongside Hülkenberg at the re-branded [[Audi in Formula One|Audi]] in {{F1|2026}}.<ref name="signing"/> He scored the team's first points as a manufacturer entrant on his Audi debut at the [[2026 Australian Grand Prix|Australian Grand Prix]], finishing ninth.<ref>{{Cite web|title=F1 star admits overtaking rivals 'by mistake' due to 'confusing' 2026 regulations|last=|date=12 March 2026|url=https://www.gpfans.com/en/f1-news/1078473/f1-gabriel-bortoleto-2026-australian-gp-confusing-regulations/|access-date=6 July 2026|website=GPFans.com|language=en}}</ref> He failed to start the following round in China after his car was withdrawn on the way to the grid with a hydraulic problem, one of four cars that did not start the race because of technical issues.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Williams' Alexander Albon and Gabriel Bortoleto of Audi also failed to start|date=15 March 2026|url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260315-both-mclarens-out-of-chinese-grand-prix-before-start|access-date=6 July 2026|website=France 24|language=en}}</ref> He finished thirteenth in Japan, twelfth in Miami, and thirteenth in Canada,<ref>{{Cite web|title=2026 Gabriel Bortoleto Driver Standings|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results/2026/drivers/GABBOR01/gabriel-bortoleto|access-date=6 July 2026|website=Formula1.com|language=en}}</ref> before a run of three consecutive eleventh-place finishes at [[2026 Monaco Grand Prix|Monaco]], the [[2026 Spanish Grand Prix|Spanish Grand Prix]] and [[2026 Austrian Grand Prix|Austria]] left him narrowly outside the points on each occasion.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Bortoleto Trusts That Audi Will Break Their Drought at Silverstone|date=1 July 2026|url=https://roundtable.io/sports/f1/news/bortoleto-trusts-that-audi-will-break-their-drought-at-silverstone|access-date=6 July 2026|website=Roundtable|language=en}}</ref> Bortoleto ended the sequence at the [[2026 British Grand Prix]], finishing eighth at Silverstone for his first points since Australia, while teammate Hülkenberg retired.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Leclerc wins dramatic British Grand Prix from Russell and Hamilton as Antonelli suffers issue|date=5 July 2026|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/leclerc-wins-dramatic-british-grand-prix-from-russell-and-hamilton-as-antonelli-suffers-issue.3bGl6laB38GIr1PfxJTNmY|access-date=6 July 2026|website=Formula1.com|language=en}}</ref> He placed eighth again at the [[2026 Belgian Grand Prix|Belgian Grand Prix]],<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-07-18 |title=F1 Results - 2026 Belgian Grand Prix |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/2026/belgian-grand-prix/results |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref> and eleventh at the [[2026 Hungarian Grand Prix|Hungarian Grand Prix]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Hungary 2026 - Result • STATS F1 |url=https://www.statsf1.com/en/2026/hongrie/classement.aspx |access-date=2026-07-26 |website=www.statsf1.com}}</ref>

== Other activities ==
In November 2025, Bortoleto launched a collection in partnership with the Brazilian brand Barthelemy.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Laloni |first=Marco |date=2025-11-23 |title=Gabriel Bortoleto lança coleção de roupas de luxo com a Barthelemy |trans-title=Gabriel Bortoleto launches luxury clothing collection with Barthelemy. |url=https://www.mktesportivo.com/2025/11/gabriel-bortoleto-lanca-colecao-de-roupas-de-luxo-com-a-barthelemy/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251129103633/https://www.mktesportivo.com/2025/11/gabriel-bortoleto-lanca-colecao-de-roupas-de-luxo-com-a-barthelemy/ |archive-date=29 November 2025 |access-date=2025-11-29 |website=MKT Esportivo |language=pt-br }}</ref> The collection features elements from the driver's time with the Trident (Formula 3), Invicta (Formula 2), and Sauber (Formula One) teams.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-11-21 |title=Anúncio de Gabriel Bortoleto fora da Sauber pega geral de surpresa |trans-title=Gabriel Bortoleto's announcement takes everyone by surprise. |url=https://velocidadetotal.com.br/anuncio-de-gabriel-bortoleto-fora-da-sauber-pega-geral-de-surpresa/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251129103413/https://velocidadetotal.com.br/anuncio-de-gabriel-bortoleto-fora-da-sauber-pega-geral-de-surpresa/ |archive-date=29 November 2025 |access-date=2025-11-29 |language=pt-BR }}</ref>

